// B2 course (B1 → B2 roadmap), module 17 „B2 kirjutamine” (b1b2-081…085), stage B2.
// Lesson template v4 (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12). One storyline, the cast a year after the B1 course
// (docs/COURSE_CAST.md): Sofia takes the B2 exam in March (the course goal: the Tartu warehouse project at Tuul
// Logistika); her course teacher Maret (Keelekool Sõna) trains the two Harno B2 writing tasks — a semi-formal or
// informal letter of ~140 words and an argumentative text or a summary with a comment of ~180 words. At the same time
// Jaan's „Kohvik Mets” opens next to Nõmme market on 18 April and needs real texts: an opinion text for Nõmme Teataja,
// letters to the district official, the coffee supplier and the neighbours, the problem–solution part of a grant
// application; Helgi retires in June after 38 years of teaching and Sofia writes the family's farewell speech.
// One goal said on the first sheet: at the end the learner writes a timed mock writing part as two real texts for the
// café opening and assesses another learner's text with a Harno-like rubric (084 Kasuta).
// New people: district official Helen Põld (Nõmme linnaosa valitsus), neighbour Ellen Pärn (68, lives next to the café),
// market trader Riho Valk, youth worker Mihkel Kangro (Nõmme noortekeskus), grant committee member Triin Laas.
// Known people: Maret (B1 module 8, B2 module 15), Annika Vaht („Kohviveski”, B2 module 11), Ingrid (district
// official), Ülle („Päevateema”), Reet Kallas (examiner, B1 module 18), Igor (B2 module 14, in the pictures).
// Grammar (B2 spiral, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md §5; no new item is assigned to this module):
//   connectors and word order after a sentence-initial bridge (Seetõttu peaks…, Kuigi …, toob see…) — 081 (notice,
//     categorize, word order), back in 083 (mistõttu, kuigi) and 084 (sõnajärg as an error type);
//   the conditional to soften a request and register (Sooviksin…, Kas saaksite…, Oleksin tänulik…; too official
//     impersonal → plain) — 082 (notice, rule table, transformation), used in 082–084 letters;
//   nominalisation -mine and cause–effect language (bussiliikluse harvenemise tõttu, selle tagajärjel, mistõttu) and the
//     conditional of solutions — 083 (notice, word forms, forms text), back in 084 (seoses avamisega);
//   government, object case and infinitives as error types with a justified correction — 084 (dialogue, notice,
//     error correction, forms text, phrase bank).
// The final shape (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B2.md §4.1 row 17, 2026-10-29): 081 LUGU R→W (corner R4 = the Linnaelu
// article with eight sentences removed and one extra, R16; main = W14 the opinion text for Nõmme Teataja), 082 KUUL L→W
// (corner L2 = Helen Põld's radio interview, ten questions with three options; main = W13 the letter to the official),
// 083 AVAS R→S (corner W2a = the youth survey chart and a summary with a comment, W15; main = S16 Jaan's talk to the grant
// committee, recorded at home), 084 PROB L→S (corner L4 = the talk show with examiner Reet Kallas and Natalja, twelve
// true / false statements; main = S16 the learner's talk at the course meeting about the corrections, recorded at home).
// Every teaching lesson: review naming the previous lesson and a module 13–15 lesson (080/073, 081/069, 082/064,
// 083/074), a pair task in the lesson, a home recording in Kasuta, two fluency tasks; S16 in 083 and 084, S17 in 081.
//   081 Maret's model opinion text (remote work); Maret's lecture on how the opinion text is assessed; the Linnaelu
//       article on grants for small cafés (sentence bank); Kasuta: car-free Sundays at Nõmme market — the readers'
//       voices, Sofia and the neighbour Ellen Pärn (argument cards), an opinion text for Nõmme Teataja.
//   082 Jaan's three drafts in the wrong tone; Helen Põld on the radio; Jaan's letter to „Kohviveski” (4-option gaps);
//       two complaints; Kasuta: three voice messages, the call to Helen Põld, the letter asking for a new deadline.
//   083 Ülle's radio interview with Mihkel Kangro (teenagers without summer work); the Linnaelu article on first jobs;
//       ranking the solutions; the survey chart and its summary; Kasuta: the grant committee — sources, the talk,
//       Triin Laas's questions and the problem–solution part of the application.
//   084 Helgi's six readings (letter to Sofia); Sofia and Jaan correct the farewell speech; Sofia's error letter; the
//       talk show; Sofia's thank-you note (forms) and Jaan's letter to the youth centre (phrase bank); Kasuta: the mock
//       writing task (a letter and invitation to the neighbours from four sources), the peer assessment, the talk.
// Lesson 5 (085) is the module's check in Harno B2 form: listening L1 (five clips, played once), L2 (Annika Vaht's
// interview), L3 (Liina Kask's talk); reading R1, R2a; writing W1 (W13) and W2a (W15, the school survey chart); speaking
// S1 (S16) and S2 (S17); every part timed with B.examPart (PART). The v3 file is in archive/v3/b2/module17.js.
// Academic value round 1 + round 2 (2026-11-03, docs/ACADEMIC_VALUE_ROUND1.md, topic map B2 row 17: kohad + ümbruskond,
// ühiskond — regions of Estonia; the writing axis stays): opener 081_d_open (census 2021: Harju 46 %, moves to / from
// Harju; Ida-Viru the most settled county, Narva; Kihnu cultural space on the UNESCO list; Saaremaa bridge plan ended
// 2023) replaces the goal text, whose storyline moved into 081_t_sit; Maret's model text 081_d_model is now a cast-free
// opinion piece on moving state jobs out of Tallinn (ERR 2019); 082_p_complaint is a parent's two letters about merging
// a village school + 082_p_know (ERR 2024: ~25 small schools); the 500–600-word problem article 083_p_article (rural
// depopulation: census 2000 / 2021, 120 000 households without fast internet, ERR 2025) with new 083_p_mc; 083_p_data
// is the real county census chart for the W2a summary (was an invented youth-centre survey); 084_p_case is a sourced
// article on the Saaremaa bridge debate; the examiner set 085_d_mono replaces 085_d_say; Ülle opens two listenings
// (082_p_lc, 084_p_show), 083_d_radio / 085_p_clips / 085_p_lc have other hosts; one retelling (081_p_say); two home
// recordings (083_t_pitch, 084_t_say); 083 Kasuta ends with the panel, so two Kasuta sheets end with a letter; the
// unsourced figures in 085_p_listen and 085_p_read are gone and the school survey 085_t_read is Kase kool's (fiction).
